{"parentUuid":"9d48b405-cd46-494c-83ed-a207c659dc78","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ba5ec24b-4d40-4ddf-ad4b-195d6e2096bb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WMsMXTdWrNxaZSc8Q4zVFd","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"body\":\"The finalize spinner starts before the deferred `progress.Finish()` runs, so on a real terminal the spinner will reuse the same line as the completed progress bar (`startSpinner` writes `\\\\r...`). That means the new \\\"keep the 100% bar visible\\\" behavior never actually takes effect here—the spinner overwrites the bar instead of rendering below it.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-05-04T19:16:10Z\",\"id\":3183903446,\"line\":266,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"This terminal-only progress/spinner transition is not covered by tests. `migrate_test.go` currently drives `migrateCheckpointsV2` with `bytes.Buffer` writers, which keeps both `startProgressBar` and `startSpinner` disabled, so the interaction that is changing here would regress without any test failing.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-05-04T19:16:11Z\",\"id\":3183903488,\"line\":266,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"### Spinner stop function erases preserved 100% progress bar\\n\\n**Medium Severity**\\n\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\\u003e\\nThe new `Finish()` logic preserves the 100% progress bar by writing a newline instead of clearing the line. However, `startSpinner` is called on the same writer *before* the deferred `Finish()` runs. The spinner's stop function (`stopFinalize(\\\"\\\")`) unconditionally executes `\\\\r\\\\033[K`, which erases the progress bar from the terminal line. When `defer progress.Finish()` then fires, it prints a newline to an already-blank line. The 100% bar is always lost — defeating the PR's stated purpose. The spinner needs to be started *after* `Finish()` preserves the bar, or `Finish()` needs to be called explicitly before the spinner begins.\\